{"search_note":"I did not find public 2024 evidence of a transparent asset-declaration release, campaign-finance disclosure, or a formal, standing mechanism showing Tinubu consistently corrected false macro claims without external fact-checking pressure.

The strongest pro-side evidence is reactive, not proactive: acknowledgment of hardship, a call for dialogue, and a late probe after abuse became visible.

The strongest anti-side evidence is concrete and repeated: inflated economic claims, protest criminalization, and legal pressure on journalists.","evidence":[{"title":"Tinubu speaks on economic reforms, new minimum wage in Democracy Day speech","publisher":"TheCable","date":"2024-06-12","url":"https://www.thecable.ng/full-text-tinubu-speaks-on-economic-reforms-new-minimum-wage-in-democracy-day-speech/","summary":"Tinubu publicly acknowledged that reforms had created hardship and said his government negotiated with labour rather than relying on arrests or repression.","question_ids":["7B.8","7B.1"]},{"title":"Tinubu seeks dialogue with protesters, asks them to suspend demonstrations","publisher":"TheCable","date":"2024-08-04","url":"https://www.thecable.ng/breaking-tinubu-asks-protesters-to-suspend-demonstrations-seeks-dialogue/","summary":"He asked protesters to pause demonstrations “to create room for dialogue” and said he had heard them “loud and clear.”","question_ids":["7B.8","7B.7"]},{"title":"Tinubu orders probe of security agents involved in arrest, detention of minors","publisher":"TheCable","date":"2024-11-04","url":"https://www.thecable.ng/tinubu-orders-probe-of-security-agents-involved-in-arrest-detention-of-minors/","summary":"After backlash, Tinubu ordered an investigation into the arrest and treatment of minors detained over the protests and directed their release.","question_ids":["7B.8","7B.7"]},{"title":"Nigeria: Freedom on the Net 2024","publisher":"Freedom House","date":"2024","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/nigeria/freedom-net/2024","summary":"Freedom House reported no nationwide internet shutdowns in 2024, which is weak positive evidence against blanket information suppression.","question_ids":["7B.8","7B.7"]},{"title":"Fact-checking president Tinubu's claims about Nigeria's economic successes in his Independence Day speech","publisher":"Africa Check","date":"2024-10-03","url":"https://africacheck.org/fact-checks/reports/fact-checking-president-tinubus-claims-about-nigerias-economic-successes-his","summary":"Africa Check found Tinubu’s claims about $30 billion in FDI and a $33 billion inherited reserve were wrong; the reserve figure was closer to $35 billion and the FDI claim was unsupported.","question_ids":["7B.8","7B.1"]},{"title":"Nigeria: Protesters Charged with Treason","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","date":"2024-09-06","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/09/06/nigeria-protesters-charged-treason","summary":"HRW said authorities charged protesters with treason, held many in prolonged detention, and framed dissent as a security threat rather than ordinary political contention.","question_ids":["7B.8","7B.7"]},{"title":"Nigeria has detained journalist who reported on corruption in widening crackdown","publisher":"Reuters via GPB","date":"2024-05-09","url":"https://www.gpb.org/news/2024/05/09/nigeria-has-detained-journalist-who-reported-on-corruption-in-widening-crackdown","summary":"Reuters reported Daniel Ojukwu was detained under the Cybercrime Act after a corruption story, which looks like punishment for investigative reporting.","question_ids":["7B.8","7B.7"]},{"title":"Nigeria police charge 4 journalists with cybercrimes for corruption reporting","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","date":"2024-10-03","url":"https://cpj.org/2024/10/nigeria-police-charge-4-journalists-with-cybercrimes-for-corruption-reporting/","summary":"CPJ reported four journalists were charged under the Cybercrimes Act despite February reforms, showing continued legal pressure on scrutiny.","question_ids":["7B.8","7B.7"]},{"title":"Nigeria considers tough penalties for subversive acts under proposed law","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","date":"2024-08-14","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/nigeria-considers-tough-penalties-for-subversive-acts-under-proposed-law-3571782","summary":"Reuters reported a Counter Subversion Bill criticized as a crackdown on dissent after the protests; the proposal itself signaled a punitive information climate.","question_ids":["7B.8","7B.7"]}]}
